<title>JAPAN: Japan two-yr note auction lowest price of 99.90.</title>
<headline>Japan two-yr note auction lowest price of 99.90.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The auction of 120 billion yen in</p>
<p>two-year government notes produced the following results, the</p>
<p>Ministry of Finance said on Thursday:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 99.90    Stop rate	   0.650 pct</p>
<p>Average price	99.94    Average yield     0.625 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   270.6 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted bids	118.0 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 47.0790 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    Feb 20, 1997   Maturity  Feb 22, 1999</p>
<p>Coupon payment     Feb 20, Aug 20</p>
</text>
